= mathed on Android

This page is laid out by the same document engine the desktop frontends use:
mathed markers through the transform, Typst's own pagination, and the CPU
rasterizer — drawn straight into an `ANativeWindow` with no GPU and no web
view in the loop.

The shell is a document. An `\app` statement reserves a slot in the page flow,
exactly as it does in emthin, and the slot is drawn where the page flow put it:

#1 Terminal #2 \app(#1, #2, 320, 180, "foot", launch: "foot")

#3 Chat #4 \app(#3, #4, 320, 180, "chat")

There is no live client to composite on Android, so a slot renders as reserved
space with its caption — the document half of emthin's model, which is the half
that is the layout authority anyway.

Math still typesets around all of it:

$ x^2 + y^2 = z^2 $

$ sum_(k=0)^n k = (n (n+1)) / 2 $

Tap anywhere to put the caret under your finger; type to edit the text. Every
edit reflows the page, and the caret follows the glyph index back to the byte
offset it came from — the same index the desktop editor uses for cursor motion.
